// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-09-24 (Thursday): Pure math sequence — the Thue-Morse sequence
// ============================================================================
//
// THE SEQUENCE: t(n) = parity of the number of 1-bits in n's binary form
// (equivalently: start from "0", repeatedly substitute 0->"01", 1->"10").
// Generation 3 (8 symbols) drives this piece:
//   gen0: 0
//   gen1: 01                       (gen1 = gen0 + NOT(gen0))
//   gen2: 0110                     (gen2 = gen1 + NOT(gen1))
//   gen3: 01101001                 (gen3 = gen2 + NOT(gen2))
// Two real, provable facts about gen3 drive the arrangement:
//   1. BALANCE — exactly four 0s and four 1s (true of every generation past
//      the first: each substitution step contributes one 0 and one 1 per
//      parent symbol, so the counts stay equal forever).
//   2. SELF-SIMILARITY — gen3's second half (positions 4-7: "1001") is the
//      exact bit-complement of its first half (positions 0-3: "0110"), by
//      the substitution rule itself (gen(n+1) = gen(n) + NOT(gen(n))).
//
// THE MUSICAL MAPPING: each of the 8 bits picks which of two phrases plays
// that cycle. Bit 0 -> M (rising call, two 3rds then a 4th: A C E -> A(oct)):
//   n("[0 ~ ~ 2 4 ~ 7 4]")   in A:minor
// Bit 1 -> M' (the exact PITCH INVERSION of M — every degree negated,
// mirrored below the tonic, identical rhythm grid, identical leap sizes
// in contrary motion):
//   n("[0 ~ ~ -2 -4 ~ -7 -4]")
// "Bit flip" in the sequence's own definition (0 -> NOT 0 = 1) becomes
// "melodic inversion" in the phrase (degree d -> -d) — the musical device
// is a direct translation of the math operation, not a decorative pairing.
// Because of fact 2 above, cycles 4-7 use exactly the M/M' assignment of
// cycles 0-3 with every phrase swapped for its opposite — the piece's own
// call-and-mirrored-answer macro-structure over its full 8 cycles performs
// the sequence's defining recursive rule, not just its digits.
// Fact 1 (four 0s, four 1s) means M and M' each get exactly 4 of the 8
// cycles — real balance, not a coincidence of the notes chosen.
// gen3 also has no three consecutive equal bits anywhere (Thue-Morse is
// famously "cube-free" — no run of length 3): audible here as the two
// back-to-back repeats (cycles 1-2 both M', cycles 5-6 both M) but never a
// third repeat in a row.
// The final cycle (bit 1, would be another M') is a cadence variant: two
// ascending 3rds (-4 -> -2 -> 0, a 5th overall) resolving home to the
// tonic instead of M's usual big low approach and retreat — marking the
// end of the generation rather than restating M' flatly a fourth time.
//
// SCALE: A:minor (aeolian) — not used on a Thursday yet (Fibonacci used C
// minor pentatonic, Collatz D harmonic minor, twin primes E phrygian,
// Pascal's triangle D dorian).
//
// ARRANGEMENT — deliberately different from the last Thursday slot
// (2026-09-17, Pascal's triangle: square lead + triangle pad + one
// euclid(3,8) kick tied to a row-sum). Today's defining fact is BINARY —
// two symbols, two mirror-image phrase-shapes — so the arrangement leans
// into "two" rather than reaching for percussion: the drone is a plain
// DYAD (scale degrees 0 and 4, tonic + 5th — exactly two notes, echoing
// the sequence's two-symbol alphabet), and there is no drum layer at all.
// Checked deliberately per MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md before deciding this: the
// piece's own rhythm already lives in the 8-step call/inversion grid and
// its rests, and the only numbers this topic actually needs an audible
// outlet for (gen3's length 8, its four 1-bits) are already spent below on
// the filter-sweep period and resonance — a kick/hat layer would be
// decorative on top of an already-complete binary structure, not something
// this specific topic calls for.
// Lead: sawtooth (rich/sharp, MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §1) for real contrast
// against the pure/soft sine drone. Filter opens across one full 8-cycle
// sweep (period = gen3's own length) so the "generation" itself is audible
// as one slow timbral arc underneath the faster call/inversion alternation;
// resonance set to 4, gen3's own count of 1-bits.
//
// CYCLES: 8 (one per bit of gen3). setcpm(24) x 8 / 60 = 20s.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(24)

$lead: n(`<
  [0 ~ ~ 2 4 ~ 7 4]
  [0 ~ ~ -2 -4 ~ -7 -4]
  [0 ~ ~ -2 -4 ~ -7 -4]
  [0 ~ ~ 2 4 ~ 7 4]
  [0 ~ ~ -2 -4 ~ -7 -4]
  [0 ~ ~ 2 4 ~ 7 4]
  [0 ~ ~ 2 4 ~ 7 4]
  [0 ~ ~ -2 -4 ~ -2 0]
>`)
  .scale("A:minor")
  .sound("sawtooth")
  .attack(.02).decay(.15).sustain(.2).release(.3)
  .lpf(sine.range(500, 2800).slow(8))
  .lpq(4)
  .sometimes(x => x.ply(2))
  .gain(.4)
  .room(1.2)

$drone: n("[0,4]").scale("A:minor")
  .sound("sine")
  .attack(1).release(2)
  .lpf(700)
  .gain(.22)
  .room(3)
